 majority is important  for two reasons one  you can override a governor's veto but  in this case a veto isn't likely since  democrats  hold the governor's mansion and both  houses of the legislature so  really the only other major thing that  requires a two-thirds vote  is raising taxes and we saw that happen  in the special session in which  democrats raised taxes with ease in the  assembly  and uh ran into trouble in the senate  they did it anyway  in the senate with a simple majority now  that of course is being challenged  in court so without that super majority  uh if it comes to tax increases they  would have to have republican  cooperation  for that and as we saw in the special  session they didn't really get that and  it looks like nicole cannizzaro will  hang on to that seat but as the top  democrat in the legislature here in  nevada that was a seat republicans  really targeted john we saw those ads  all over tv  a lot of attention poured onto that one  and it's interesting because one of the  things that was talked about  in the special session over the summer  was police reform bills that  might get passed up in carson city  canazarro has a lot of strong support  from  police unions and lobbyists they played  a big role in those bills back in 2019  she's a deputy district attorney in  clark county as well so we'll see how  all that plays out when the legislature  is back in session vanessa  well the clark county school district  board of trustees is about to have a new  look as well if the results hold it will  have three new faces  and all of the members will be women in  district a lisa guzman has a lead over  liberty  levitt in district b vocal trump  supporter katie williams has beaten jeff  profit evelyn garcia morales leads  tamika henry in district c  it appears school board president lola  brooks is keeping her seat  she leads teacher alexis salt in  district e  8 news now reporter kristen drummond  spoke with the presumptive winners about  the e